  sections={[
    {
      h2: 'What Wim Hof breathing is',
      paras: [
        "One round has three parts. First you take 30 deep breaths in a row: a full inhale through the nose or mouth, pushing the belly out, then letting it go without force. After the last exhale you hold your breath with empty lungs. That's the retention. When it ends you take one big breath in, hold it for 15 seconds and let it go. That's the recovery breath, and it closes the round.",
        "The official instructions say to repeat that three to four times, and to hold the retention until you feel the urge to breathe. They also mention lightheadedness and tingling in the fingers and feet.",
        "Refresher is not affiliated with Wim Hof or with WHM Services, which publishes the official Wim Hof Method app. In Refresher the technique is listed as Power Breath by Wim Hof, alongside box, 4-7-8 and coherent breathing on the same pacer.",
